    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d493">

                <pb facs="0745" n="631" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg631"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">551.5G1/13: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Dawes</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract—Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-11-04T17:00:00+00:00">November 4, 1931—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 4—4:25 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>429.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>With reference to the proposal for a conference on silver, Mr. MacDonald
                    manifested a prejudice against the calling of any conference in which the views
                    of Great Britain did not coincide with those of the United States.</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Dawes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
